Package: resize-gpu-bars
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, bash (>= 5), pciutils, kmod, systemd
Recommends: initramfs-tools, grub2-common
Description: Resizable BAR setup and bind guard for AMD GPUs on Mac Pro 7,1
 Enlarges the CPU-visible VRAM aperture (BAR0) of every AMD GPU to the
 largest size the device supports, re-enumerates only the PCI subtrees that
 contain GPUs so the kernel re-sizes the bridge windows, and loads amdgpu
 once behind a guard that never hands the driver a device with an
 unassigned BAR (which would hang the boot in an SR-IOV mailbox wait).
 .
 Discovers GPUs, Resizable BAR registers and bridge topology at run time,
 so any mix of MPX cards and other PCIe devices is supported.
